The  command  configures  memory disk devices.  It will associate
the special file with a range of user‐virtual memory allocated by
the process itself.  The command should be run in the background.
If successful, the command will not return.  Otherwise, an  error
message  will be printed.  To "unconfigure" the memory disk, just
kill the background process started earlier.  Configures the mem‐
ory disk with one megabyte of user‐space memory.  The special de‐
vice will become inoperative if the process is killed  while  the
special device is open.
